{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelLevel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelLevel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_two_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_two_even","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L148-L151","doc":"Level `2`, even index: `exponent(2, 2m) = m(m−1)`. The concrete C1 case: with\n`n = 2m` this is `≈ n²/4`, the number the S1 growth-budget probe uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.two_mul_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L136-L146","doc":"`2·C(m,2) = m(m−1)` — the standard identity, in the `ℕ`-subtraction form needed\nbelow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_mul","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**Degree law on the level lattice.** At `n = d·m` the exponent is exactly `d·C(m,2)`,\nwhich is the `q^{n²/2d}` growth: `d·C(m,2) = d·m(m−1)/2 ≈ (d·m)²/(2d)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_one_rec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_one_rec","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L117-L120","doc":"Specialization to level `1`, recovering `qBorelKernel_succ`'s shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_rec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_rec","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L111-L115","doc":"**The RSZ kernel family relation** `tₙ = q^{n−d} · t_{n−d}` — the defining property of\nthe level-`d` q-Borel kernel, for every `d ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_one_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_one_eq","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**Level `1` reproduces the existing kernel on the nose.** This is the compatibility\ncheck: the generalization is conservative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L101-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelKernelLevel","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L98-L99","doc":"**The level-`d` q-Borel kernel** `tₙ = q^{exponent(d,n)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_rec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_rec","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L80-L96","doc":"**The RSZ exponent recurrence**, proved from the closed form:\n`exponent(d,n) = (n−d) + exponent(d, n−d)` for `d ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_one_eq_choose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_one_eq_choose","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L76-L78","doc":"At level `1` the exponent is the Jacobi-theta exponent `C(n,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Below the level, the kernel exponent vanishes: the chain is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernel.qBorelExp","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QBorelKernelLevel.lean#L68-L70","doc":"**The level-`d` q-Borel kernel exponent.** With `n = d·m + r` (`m = n / d`,\n`r = n % d`), summing the chain `n, n−d, …, r` gives `m·r + d·C(m,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}